<section><div class="wrap feature-lead"><div class="feature-copy"><span class="section-tag">The same useful view</span><h2>Your Mac becomes the battery dashboard.</h2><p>WhatBattery uses the diagnostics connection Finder already understands. After the one-time trust step, a supported iPhone or iPad appears in the app with the same health maths used for the Mac.</p><ul class="benefit-list"><li>Health and raw capacity</li><li>Cycle count and charge state</li><li>Temperature, voltage, and live power</li><li>USB or Wi-Fi after the first pairing</li><li>No device-side app or account</li></ul></div><img src="/img/screenshot-idevice.png" alt="WhatBattery showing a connected iPad's battery health, cycles, charge, temperature, voltage, and live power" width="440" /></div></section>

<section class="soft-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-tag">Three steps</span><h2>Pair once. Read whenever the device is available.</h2></div><div class="card-grid"><article class="card"><div class="card-icon">1</div><h3>Connect with a cable</h3><p>Unlock the device and tap Trust. The first pairing cannot be completed wirelessly.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="card-icon">2</div><h3>Enable Wi-Fi visibility</h3><p>In Finder, choose “Show this iPhone when on Wi-Fi” and apply the setting.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="card-icon">3</div><h3>Open the device tab</h3><p>WhatBattery reads the available battery data. If iOS changes a field, it reports the device as unreadable rather than showing a bogus number.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section><div class="wrap narrow prose"><div class="callout"><strong>Compatibility note:</strong> the diagnostics relay is an undocumented Apple interface. WhatBattery validates the data it receives and degrades cleanly if a future iOS release changes the fields. This capability requires a Developer ID build and is one reason the app is distributed outside the Mac App Store.</div><p><a href="/docs/iphone-ipad/">Follow the complete USB and Wi-Fi setup guide →</a></p></div></section>

